-- 050_golf_polos_batch_2.sql
-- 2026-08-31. Golf polos batch 2: tops_61 - tops_99. Thirty-nine garments, 82 photographs.
--
-- COUNT, done before a single row was written. 86 files in Downloads\Golf Polos: 83 JPG + 3 PNG.
-- Four of the JPGs (the 06:22 shots) are BYTE-IDENTICAL by MD5 to photos already filed as
-- tops_57_..._01_hanger / _02_label and tops_58_..._01_hanger / _02_label. They are batch-1
-- re-downloads, excluded. The three PNGs are not screenshots: they are one garment (flat-lay,
-- neck label, chest detail) - the Bermuda Sands bird-print polo, tops_99.
-- 82 photographs remain. Grouped by shot order into 39 garments: 40 flat-lays and 42
-- label/detail shots, confirmed on a labelled contact sheet before any insert.
--
-- TWO RED PETER MILLAR "INTERCLUB" POLOS, NOT ONE (tops_62 and tops_64). Same white RSGC
-- crown-and-monogram with INTERCLUB beneath, same Summer Comfort neck label. The size tags
-- differ and both were read at full resolution: S on tops_62, M on tops_64. Confirmed with Max
-- before writing. If they ever turn out to be one garment, tops_64 is the one to retire.
--
-- ONE FLAT-LAY IS TWO FRAMES. tops_71 was shot twice 0.2s apart (070405412 / 070405597). Both
-- are filed, as _01_hanger and _02_hanger.
--
-- SIZING. The batch-1 rule holds and is now much better evidenced. Every US golf brand that
-- could be read comes in S or M and nothing is larger: FootJoy S/M/M/M, Nike Golf S and S,
-- Peter Millar S/M/M, Fairway & Greene M, Greyson S, G/FORE M, Glenmuir S/M/M/S, adidas S.
-- Buy S in US golf brands, M in generic and Asian-sized. Eighteen sizes could not be read and
-- are recorded as unknown rather than inferred from the rule.
--
-- CLUBS. This batch is the first that is NOT mostly Royal Sydney. Home clubs: eleven RSGC and
-- two Woollahra ("REPRESENTATIVE", tops_78 and tops_91) - no restriction anywhere. Visitor
-- souvenirs, which carry another club's crest and should be worn accordingly: Royal Melbourne
-- (tops_73), Barnbougle Lost Farm (tops_72), Barnbougle Dunes (tops_97), Ocean Dunes King
-- Island (tops_96), Golf Club Barbaroux (tops_92), Camiral (tops_94), Bonville (tops_95),
-- Links Hope Island (tops_99), and the Masters (tops_85).
--
-- BRANDS NOT GUESSED. Nine rows carry no brand: tops_61, tops_72, tops_73, tops_78, tops_80,
-- tops_86, tops_92, tops_93 and the second Nike-style chest mark on tops_71. In each case the
-- neck label is either absent from the frame, blacked out, or unreadable at full resolution
-- after zoom. Following tops_58: do not guess a brand into these rows.
--
-- ONE I NEARLY GOT WRONG. tops_94 reads as a Nike swoosh on a contact sheet. At full
-- resolution the neck label is G/FORE, size M, and what looked like a swoosh is a camo shape.
-- The chest reads CAMIRAL. Zoom before naming a brand off a thumbnail.
--
-- COLOUR. Measured against the white table in frame, batch-1 method, with ONE CORRECTION that
-- matters: the white-point candidates now EXCLUDE the garment's own box. On the first pass the
-- pale garments were their own white reference, which turned the khaki FootJoy neutral grey and
-- the peach Under Armour into a warm grey. The reference is the table, never the garment.
-- Ten near-white garments are still set by judgement and flagged derived, exactly as tops_52
-- and tops_53 were: the method measures shadow on a white piqué, not colour.
--
-- CONDITION. Asserted only from the flat, evenly-lit flat-lays, per the hats lesson. Nothing
-- was inspected by hand. Two rows carry a possible-mark note rather than a damage claim.

